# Phase 6 Walkthrough: MAPPO + Temporal Transformer + Graph Attention Network (GAT)

Phase 6 extends the SAGE-Traffic multi-agent traffic control framework by integrating a genuine trainable **Graph Attention Network (GAT)** layer over the four-intersection road network graph (A, B, C, D), operating on top of Phase 5's **Temporal Transformer Encoder**.

$$\text{History } [4, 43\text{-D}] \xrightarrow{\text{Transformer}} [4, 64\text{-D}] \xrightarrow{\text{GAT (Physical Adjacency)}} [4, 64\text{-D}] \xrightarrow{} \begin{cases} \text{Actor } (64+4=68\text{-D}) \to \pi(a|h'_i, \text{id}_i) \\ \text{Critic } (4 \times 64 = 256\text{-D}) \to V(S_{\text{gat}}) \end{cases}$$

---

## 1. Architectural Implementation

### Physical Graph Topology
Derived directly from the SUMO road network in [`network/build_network.py`](file:///c:/Users/kashi/OneDrive/Desktop/major/network/build_network.py):
- **Nodes**: Intersections A (top-left), B (top-right), C (bottom-left), D (bottom-right).
- **Physical Bidirectional Corridors**: $A \leftrightarrow B$, $A \leftrightarrow C$, $B \leftrightarrow D$, $C \leftrightarrow D$.
- **Disallowed Non-Neighbor Connections**: Diagonals $A \leftrightarrow D$ and $B \leftrightarrow C$ do not exist physically and are strictly masked with $-10^9$ logits, ensuring $\alpha_{ij} \equiv 0.0$.
- **Self-Loops**: Configurable (`add_self_loops: true`), allowing each intersection to attend to its own temporal state alongside physical neighbors.

### Multi-Head GAT Layer ([`models/gat_network.py`](file:///c:/Users/kashi/OneDrive/Desktop/major/models/gat_network.py))
- Input: $[B, 4, 64]$ temporal node embeddings from the Transformer encoder.
- Multi-Head Attention: $K=4$ heads, learnable projection $W^k \in \mathbb{R}^{64 \times 64}$, attention vectors $\mathbf{a}_{\text{src}}^k, \mathbf{a}_{\text{dst}}^k \in \mathbb{R}^{64}$.
- Normalized Attention: $\alpha_{ij}^k = \frac{\exp(e_{ij}^k)}{\sum_{l \in \mathcal{N}(i)} \exp(e_{il}^k)}$ where $\sum_{j \in \mathcal{N}(i)} \alpha_{ij}^k = 1.0$.
- Head Aggregation: Head averaging (`concat_heads: false`) preserves 64-D node representations.
- Actor: Decentralized, receiving strictly its local 64-D GAT embedding + 4-D agent ID = 68-D ($68 \to 64 \to 64 \to 4$).
- Centralized Critic: Receives concatenated $4 \times 64 = 256$-D representation ($256 \to 128 \to 64 \to 1$), training-only.

